module

public import CatCrypt.Quantum.AndAncilla

/-!
# Uncomputation with a decidable qfree and permeable check

Uncomputation of a clean ancilla (Bennett's compute; use; uncompute, as in Silq, Unqomp and
Qrisp) is sound when the block computing the ancilla is *qfree* (it maps basis states to
phased basis states) and *permeable* on its inputs (it commutes with `Z` there), and the block
using the ancilla is permeable on the ancilla and the inputs. Qrisp declares both properties;
here they are Boolean checks on lists of reversible atoms `RevOp n` with soundness theorems.

A syntactic qfree test on `List (Gate n)` is too weak, since the Toffoli decomposition
`toffoliGates` contains Hadamard gates. The checks therefore run on atoms: single gates, the
multi-controlled `X` (lowered by `mctrlGates`) and the relative-phase Toffoli (lowered by
`rtofGates`), each with an exact gate list and an inverse.

The matrix of a gate list is `QFT.listMatrix` (head gate applied first); `P₀ a`, `P₁ a` and
`X_a` below are `embedGate1 n a proj0`, `embedGate1 n a proj1` and `embedGate1 n a pauliX`.

## Main definitions

* `RevOp n` — the reversible atoms; `RevOp.gates` their lowering, `RevOp.inv` their inverses,
  `revGates` the lowering of a list.
* `Gate.qfree`, `Gate.permeable q`, `RevOp.qfree`, `RevOp.permeable q`, `RevOp.within S` — the
  per-atom checks.
* `uncomputable a ins C U` — the check for compute `C` into the ancilla `a` from the inputs
  `ins`, then use `U`.
* `PhaseGen S` — phases generated by diagonal single-qubit operators on the qubits `S`.
* `RevForm a ins M` — `M = D (1 + Π (X_a - 1))` with `D` a phase on `a :: ins` and `Π` a
  predicate projector on `ins`: the matrix writes a Boolean function of `ins` into `a`.

## Main results

* `RevOp.commute_Z_of_permeable` — a permeable atom commutes with `Z` on the qubit.
* `branch_of_permeable` — a list permeable on `a` is a two-branch matrix on `a`.
* `computes_of_check` — a list passing the compute check writes a predicate of the inputs into
  the ancilla up to a phase, in the form `listMatrix_predAncilla_conj` takes.
* `listMatrix_uncompute` — compute; use; uncompute restores the ancilla to `|0⟩` and applies
  the branch of the use block selected by the predicate.
* `listMatrix_uncompute_ctrl` — with the use block controlled on the ancilla, the result is the
  clean controlled program, by `listMatrix_predAncilla_conj` and `predAncilla_restores`.
* `uncomputable_mcx`, `uncomputable_rtof` — the multi-controlled `X` and the relative-phase
  Toffoli pass the check.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

open scoped Matrix
open CatCrypt.Quantum.QCircuit
open CatCrypt.Quantum.GateUnitarity
open CatCrypt.Quantum.Programs.Qubit
open CatCrypt.Quantum.Optimization.DisjointCommute
open CatCrypt.Quantum.Optimization.MixedCommute
open CatCrypt.Quantum.ControlledGates
